golden temples beautiful beaches  bustling night markets Thailand has long  been a world-famous tourist destination  it's expecting a record number of 40  million visitors in 2019 well over half  the country's population and it's  dependent on tourist dollars it accounts  for about 20 percent of GDP but the  industry barely existed before 1960 its  origins were in fact born out of a dark  passage of American history here's how  war made Thailand a tourist destination  [Music]  the Vietnam War saw over 3 million  American soldiers sent to Southeast Asia  many would be stationed in Thailand  which became a major ally in the region  and home to seven US air bases at the  height of the conflict some 50,000  military personnel was stationed  throughout Thailand as America's  involvement in Vietnam deepened more  resources were pumped into the support  network in Thailand  as well as building highways and ports  the u.s. sent aid for other  infrastructure and social projects  aiming to improve living standards and  combat the spread of communism  all the while Thailand's capital Bangkok  became a center for air travel as  international airlines founded a  convenient location to refuel it was  here in Bangkok where many American  soldiers headed for rest and  recuperation for R&amp;R days thousands of  colored neon signs proclaimed the city's  bars bath houses massage parlors and  dozens of luxurious nightclubs each with  its pretty Thai hostesses the notorious  red-light districts were hard to resist  for soldiers who'd spent months and  during the terror of the jungle  [Music]  the US soldiers were also big spenders  handing over almost 11 million dollars  in 1967 that's around 22 percent of  total expenditure by foreign visitors  and as the number of soldiers and other  visitors began to rise tourism  infrastructure increased to plush  air-conditioned hotels abound and new  shoe box style office buildings dominate  the skyline in the helter-skelter  transformation of what was once a sedate  oriental port  if the war ended in 1975 the number of  tourists dropped but only briefly the  industry will go from strength to  strength in the following decades the  infrastructure built for US soldiers and  businesses had a cost of over 1.6  billion dollars in military and aids  spending created the foundation for  today's Thai tourism industry in 2018  Thailand is expected to make 63 billion  dollars from tourism but Americans are  no longer the big spenders anymore  another superpower has taken that title  the Chinese  [Music]  you
 

